{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift","id":1415551,"title":"I'm too scared to shift","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-26T08:41:53-07:00","id":1415551,"title":"I'm too scared to shift","content":"Some background first. I am ST a Werewolf The Wild West game, set in 1880. The Pack is 5 Players, with one with experience with WoD, and a second that has played VtM some. The other three Players are new to WoD. Now when I started the game, it's been running for almost 6 months once a week, I decided it would be better to have a single Tribe Sept/Caern. I let the Players decide what Tribe, which they decided Uktena. The Pack has one member for each Auspice. While making the characters I let them use Merits and Flaws. The experienced player decided that his character has the Flaws of Insane Ancestor, and Derangement: Multiple Personality. Now here is the point of this post----this player decided that his non Homid forms is tied with Insane Ancestor and Multiple Personality......when he goes Lupus or Hispo his Insane Ancestor screams in horror in his head due to his Ancestor being killed by a wolf. And his Glabro form triggers his second Personality. With these things, that player refuses to have his character shift into any other form. And yes, he hasn't utilitized the benefits of Ancestors so far either. To be honest, these flaws really haven't been brought up in the 6 months of gaming, only that he refuses to shift. Now, the heart of the post......In Game, what ramifications would a Garou who refuses to shift face from the Sept, the Elders? I will admit....in my decade plus experience for ST Werewolf, this situation is a new one for me and I am not sure who to handle it. The Pack has gotten the Renown that they are bout ready to gain Rank Two ....but I am feeling that a Garou who refuses to shift would denied further advancement simply because he hasn't gained the insight for utilizing the Blessing that Gaia and Luna have bestowed on him.....but I am hoping for further or different thoughts on this topic and a good route to deal with it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:53:46-07:00","id":1415556,"title":"","content":"Someone who would be afraid to even shift wouldn't even be considered part of any Tribe in the first place IIRC. They'd still be considered just a pup who don't have what it takes to pass the Rite of Passage. He might as well as be a Kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:58:04-07:00","id":1415557,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a part of the litany about not dealing with the sick, either physically or mentally? Why wasn't the pc culled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T09:06:08-07:00","id":1415559,"title":"","content":"Well tbh, I dropped the ball on that. I started the game after the Rite of Passage, and didn't bother role playing the Rite. Which that in itself isn't that big of a deal. Where i dropped the ball was when I didn't thoroughly looked over and discussed the characters with the players, and the Flaws of the Player wasn't brought to my attention till over a month of play. And I went ahead and let it slide due to how long the game had been going. So now I am looking for a in game way to deal with it. <br /> <br /> One way I am thinking bout dealing with it is that the Pack as whole, will not be allowed to Rank up till they have resolved that issue in game....aka Umbra Quest to Tribelands to resolve the issue with the Insane Ancestor....peacefully or violently....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T09:19:47-07:00","id":1415560,"title":"","content":"Also the character itself doesn't make sense. How could his ancestor be killed by a common wolf so easily? Was it a Lupus-born in actuality? Because the latter would make much more sense entirely. Or is this ancestor just some common human or a Kinfolk? If any of those I sincerely doubt those two types of beings would still be around, coherent, or able to project inside your player's head when ever he shifts. It doesn't make sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T10:43:33-07:00","id":1415573,"title":"","content":"Sadly repeat that i dropped the ball with this. The player knows enough bout werewolf to make a character, but it is becoming apparent that he doesn't know the intricate details. Living in a small town (5k pop) that is 3hrs to any major city, has gotten me wanting to try to work this character out and smooth it up and not loosing a player....due to the rarity of players in the area lol. I will admit that he hasn't hash out the details bout all that...the flaws...but I am waiting for him to clarify them. I hate to say it but I might have to trash the Chronicle and start from scratch. Which now that I think bout it, wouldn't be that bad. It would give the inexperience players to make a character that is more to there liking since they have become familiar with the Werewolf. Just hate to drop the story I am going through lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T11:10:11-07:00","id":1415575,"title":"","content":"Don't drop the story, just go with your original hook and have the pack go into the Middle-Umbra to try and resolve the ancestor of the &quot;crazy&quot; PC so he can shift without fear anymore. Though if it really is that bad and you can't reconcile the error of that particular PC and want to &quot;trash&quot; the Chronicle altogether, just have early Pentex (Premium Oil as this Chronicle is set in 1880 as you say) begin to have interest where the Caern of the Tribe is at due to some surveyors realizing a huge oil reservoir is there. Have the Premium Oil Agents backed with OP Fomori, Banes, silver bulletry just wipe out the entire Tribe. Make sure all your PCs die heroic deaths trying to stave off the brutal and ugly manifest destiny of Premium Oil to the last Uktena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 09-26-2020, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T11:54:34-07:00","id":1415581,"title":"","content":"Lol surprisingly that Premium Oil hook could work due to me setting the Chronicle in SouthEastern Oklahoma, right at Red River. There has been oil rigs here in S.E. Okla and N.E. Tex.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T12:14:33-07:00","id":1415585,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as I read it, the Crinos form is still an option, right?<br /> So,his pack isn't supposed to suffer his sickness, or something, so he is kind of save if his unwillingness to shift doesn't inconvenience the rest of the pack, community and so on. But, there are Rites of other circumstances, where he has to shift, and in this cases he might have to suck it up...<br /> I mean, screams in the head are possibly a rais in difficulty for some actions, but not that much of a problem, if the character really needs to be a wold or hispo....<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, the concept is kind of unrealistic....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T12:59:53-07:00","id":1415588,"title":"","content":"This player refuses for his character to shift, even to Crinos. I had a situation where the Pack was blown up with dynamite, and the Insane Ancestor Player got in a huff because he is Homid and he can't regenerate while in Breed form. And the Pack had to travel 15 miles to a location but couldn't use horses....and the other night the Pack encountered a Golem. The Insane Ancestor is designed to be a knife fighter, and when he struck the Golem with his knife it really didn't anything....so he decided he was useless for the fight. The worst part the Pack enables his behavior due to them being new to Werewolf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T13:52:31-07:00","id":1415594,"title":"","content":"It's not a crime not to shift. But refusal to shift at all indicates either the character is ashamed of being a werewolf, or has some other major problem. It also means he has abandoned a major way he can defend the sept if it is attacked. These would all likely be Renown hits in Honor (and in some cases, perhaps Wisdom or Glory). And it would probably provoke the Garou in the sept to put assign Rank challenges that would require him to shift. And since he won't, he'll fail them and stay the Rank he is (or eventually lose so much Honor he'll go down one if he's already above Cliath). And over time, the rest of the Garou will increasingly treat him with contempt, making him the effective sept omega. That can be brutal.<br /> <br /> I'd simply have the player suffer the consequences of his decisions. When the PCs had enough, he can start acting differently and perhaps go on that quest you've developed to deal with his Insane Ancestor.<br /> <br /> So my advice is to stop seeing this as a problem, and more of an opportunity for roleplay and to explore Garou society. Just be up front with the Player (not his PC) that you'll start having the NPCs react this way, and if he wants that to change, then his PC needs to start developing a different attitude. But once the PC is ready, you're prepared to help him. Who knows, perhaps he wants to see the sept and other Garou treat him badly as a result because of the RP opportunities it presents, or enjoy the challenges not shifting represents for him.<br /> <br /> So have a brief out-of-character discussion with him so you can level set, and then proceed. You'll know either to proceed with your plot up front, or to hold that in reserve until the Player is ready for it.<br /> <br /> (And maybe an initial solution isn't that the insane ancestor is purged and he can shift all the time; but that he is somehow able to shift into one form initially. And the other forms require other quests. Or some combination. Be prepared to be flexible.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:07:28-07:00","id":1415596,"title":"","content":"I think it might be worth talking to this play about the actual mechanics of the Flaws in question.<br /> <br /> For example, he doesn't get to say specifically when the Flaw kicks in, you do. It's not automatic that he gets to define it as &quot;shifting to X forms,&quot; and then every time he shifts, it happens. Esp. since there's a roll attached even if you decide it should kick in.<br /> <br /> The Derangement can be suppressed for by spending 1 WP.<br /> <br /> This character can be made functional, if the player is actually going to abide by the rules instead of playing the Flaws in question as far more punitive than they actually are. If necessary, there are Rites and Gifts that can heal Derangements if you just want to get rid of that by a higher Ranking Garou stepping in and doing it. Swap the Flaw to owning a favor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:50:33-07:00","id":1415604,"title":"","content":"Looking through the books that I have access too, and I will admit that I haven't found any Rites or Gifts to deal with Derangements. I figured there would be, but I don't know anything bout them. Y'all mind pointing me in the right direction where I might can find them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: btw I have been toying with the idea of having a Choctaw Medicine Folk (Aka Dreamspeaker, coz the Pack and Sept are Choctaw Uktena) with Knowledge in Mind Sphere to abolish the Derangement. That's more of a &quot;last straw&quot; type idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","user":"Mahjemm01","date":". 09-26-2020, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T15:34:41-07:00","id":1415615,"title":"","content":"Yep, Awakened with spheres in Mind can definitely help him. I'd say it'll need to be someone with atleast Mind 4 or 5 to aid with that though. After that the shaman would have to gather at least as much Arete successes as that PC's willpower. Another alternative route would to have that shaman just convene with that ancestor (or even maybe just a Theurge that isn't a Mage, they can speak with spirits too) use the Spirit Sphere and try and fix its &quot;pain&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 09-26-2020, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T16:27:49-07:00","id":1415620,"title":"","content":"When I was talking bout the Medicine Folk I was strictly talking bout purging the Player Garou of his Derangement: Multiple Personality.....Coz besides having a Insane Past Life that screams at him he also has Multiple Personalities on top of the Insane Past Life....<br /> <br /> And since the Shaman would be a NPC, there is no reason why it wouldn't have Mind of at least 4 along with Spirit dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T05:34:41-07:00","id":1415676,"title":"","content":"I think from my experience that there are many ways to handle it:<br /> 1. Most traditional Garou will likely try to eliminate him as weak (as Litany says, read Valkenburg Foundation opening story as an inspiration).<br /> 2. It will severly hits his Renown (ignoring the wolf part of the nature).<br /> So most likely he will be an Omega in his pack (somebody has to).<br /> Resolution of this problem<br /> 1. Valkenburg Foundation (some sort of an asylum for deranged garou).<br /> 2. Powerful entity with mind altering abilities could help (as Mage with Mind Sphere mentioned above could help). Of course it left you with the ancestors problem.<br /> 3. Quest to umbral Legendary Realm (to solve the ancestor problem) and/or to Summer Country (it is believed that there mental disabilities could be healed).<br /> Or, if you plan to run a longer story and like heroic stories you could not let his character heal himself, mock and hurt this character for the entire story and, at the end, use this flaws as an advantage (like during a great battle for the caern when everyone shifts into crinos/hispo and him making his way to the enemy camp, his flaws preventing him from raging, and turn the enemy artillery against him... or his septmates if they went too far). Hell, I almost see it, BSD fighting his pack, fomori shooting the cannons, and this character, who says them that there will be a new target. Fomori let him aim the cannon and...<br /> <br /> &quot;BSD is chasing your Kinfolk brother/sister/father/mother in crinos. He/she runs and then he/she trips. It's only a matter of seconds for BSD to get him/her...&quot;<br /> &quot;You see Raging Fire, this big f@#$%*g Ahroun, who first called you a coward for many moons and then took your Kinfolk lover for himself. She couldn't say no, the Elders decided that Raging Fire will be a better mate for her. And now, he is a hero again, standing over 2 BSD corpses. Right in front of your cannon. Noone will know. And, if you will be lucky enough (and years of using the homid form let you hone your gunnery skills) you could also hits at least two of those Elders...&quot;<br /> And, to satisfy my need for tearful endings, let him be crucial for victory (if he didn't start to shoot his septmates) and then accuse him of helping the Wyrm (someone saw him using the cannon with fomori around him).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 09-27-2020, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T20:33:35-07:00","id":1415777,"title":"","content":"The character is a basketcase. If the sept is very nice and lenient he's getting shipped of to Valkenburg for a lot of treatment.<br /> <br /> Or just dump him in Erebus for 6 months if they're not as cuddly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T02:42:31-07:00","id":1415790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1415777#post1415777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or just dump him in Erebus for 6 months if they're not as cuddly.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't do that. First of all Erebus is for sinners who should be punished and cleansed, not for lunatics. He didn't do something wrong so he cannot be send there. Second it's not a Garou decision for how long the punished will be kept there. It's Charyss, the ruler of the realm, who decides if the sinner is cleansed.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Valkenburg Foundation is also out of question. I thought it was established in the 80's of XIX century. But my &quot;spider sense&quot; was tingling so I checked. I was wrong: the first entry in Valkenburg's journal is 20 January 1913.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T02:53:46-07:00","id":1415792,"title":"","content":"Here is a simple solution, put focus on interacting with the wolf half of the garou.<br /> <br /> Maybe the pack is sent to parlay with a Red Talon and Wendigo run sept? Maybe they have to take a criminal to wolf-home?<br /> <br /> If he has managed in homid so far, put him in situations where he -has- to rely on other forms.<br /> <br /> Also, as an ooc solution, ask the player if they want to play A werewolf at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T14:04:53-07:00","id":1415884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1415790#post1415790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can't do that. First of all Erebus is for sinners who should be punished and cleansed, not for lunatics. He didn't do something wrong so he cannot be send there. Second it's not a Garou decision for how long the punished will be kept there. It's Charyss, the ruler of the realm, who decides if the sinner is cleansed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is split personality as well as the insane ancestor could be indicators of impurity. It is the &quot;guards&quot; in Erebus who tie themselves to their charge and treat/torture the garou there.<br /> That's why garou usually see this real as Hell and little is publicly known about it's healing qualities, for few return...<br /> <br /> Talking to the player seems like a good idea.<br /> Besides that, there is a simple solution: death.<br /> If separated and faced with an enemy the character has a problem. Books are unclear if homid can in breedform soak agg damage (depending on edition), in any case there is no regeneration and few dice to fight back...<br /> <br /> Also, shapeshifting is mandatory in Frenzy. His fear of what happens when he shifts, plus any other external stress factor might warrant a rage roll for frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T15:51:11-07:00","id":1415896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1415884#post1415884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is split personality as well as the insane ancestor could be indicators of impurity. It is the &amp;quot;guards&amp;quot; in Erebus who tie themselves to their charge and treat/torture the garou there.<br /> That's why garou usually see this real as Hell and little is publicly known about it's healing qualities, for few return...<br /> <br /> Talking to the player seems like a good idea.<br /> Besides that, there is a simple solution: death.<br /> If separated and faced with an enemy the character has a problem. Books are unclear if homid can in breedform soak agg damage (depending on edition), in any case there is no regeneration and few dice to fight back...<br /> <br /> Also, shapeshifting is mandatory in Frenzy. His fear of what happens when he shifts, plus any other external stress factor might warrant a rage roll for frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it could indicate impurity. The problem is that he is not tainted. Only wrong in the head. Remember that there are only two ways to punish someone in Erebus: losing The Deal or Rite of the Silver Forge. The first one requires the character's presence in Erebus (I doubt that he will go there volountarily) the second one is reserved for the biggest sinner who otherwise escaped the punishment (I know only 2 characters who ended there, one is Wyrm Eater, Uktena from a short introduction story in Erebus part of Umbra: The Velvet Shadow 1st edition, the second one is Spike Stealer, an Iron Rider from one of the story ideas from the same book; both guilty of destroying the caern). So I believe that it would be very unfair to send the flawed Garou there and it could lead Master of the Rite ending there instead. Not to mention that not many Garou know this rite. I think that this character's flaws should be used to create many role play oportunities. Or, if we treat him as tainted, should be cast out of the sept. Problem solved. Either this player will have to create a new character or play solo. BTW, what kind of ST allows to create a character like that if he cannot deal with the consequences?<br /> <br /> As for raging you are right... if we follow the rules. But I would rather use a golden rule and allow the character go berserk (with all advantages and disadvantages) not changing the form. And role play it to the bone (maybe creating a hole in his soul for Wyrm to fill it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T02:37:18-07:00","id":1415956,"title":"","content":"I feel talking to the player about it ooc would be the best solution, because their lack of shifting could be from few things;<br /> <br /> A) They want to challenge themselves by relying ONLY in homid form.<br /> <br /> B) They don't actually want to play a werewolf and would be a-ok playing kinfolk.<br /> <br /> C) They aren't comfortable portraying a non-human to the level that garou requires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T12:37:09-07:00","id":1416750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1415896#post1415896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it could indicate impurity. The problem is that he is not tainted. Only wrong in the head. Remember that there are only two ways to punish someone in Erebus: losing The Deal or Rite of the Silver Forge. The first one requires the character's presence in Erebus (I doubt that he will go there volountarily) the second one is reserved for the biggest sinner who otherwise escaped the punishment (I know only 2 characters who ended there, one is Wyrm Eater, Uktena from a short introduction story in Erebus part of Umbra: The Velvet Shadow 1st edition, the second one is Spike Stealer, an Iron Rider from one of the story ideas from the same book; both guilty of destroying the caern). So I believe that it would be very unfair to send the flawed Garou there and it could lead Master of the Rite ending there instead. Not to mention that not many Garou know this rite. I think that this character's flaws should be used to create many role play opportunities. Or, if we treat him as tainted, should be cast out of the sept. Problem solved. Either this player will have to create a new character or play solo. BTW, what kind of ST allows to create a character like that if he cannot deal with the consequences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, the taint isn't relevant for Erebus, since taint can be removed by &quot;Rite of Cleansing&quot; and other means, but an underlying impurity or even corruption can't.<br /> Also, it would be perfectly acceptable, to tie someone up, walk him to the gate of Erebus and throw him past the three-headed dog. As per the rules, the three-headed dog would not allow that person to leave Erebus again through its entrance, and the person once freed from his bonds would still need to travel through the entire Realm in search of the silver lake to exit. And plenty of guards on the way to offer &quot;The Deal&quot;. As far as I remember, they can be quite persuasive or forceful when offering the deal, so that chances are good, the person doesn't make it out.<br /> <br /> But, since the healing properties of Erebus are relatively unknown and it is regarded more like a hell by most garou (at least in the 1st Umbra book, iirc) it is unlikely that someone would do this.<br /> <br /> Also, most garou might try to heal such an afflicted garou. Not, themselves, but there are spirits, and therapists among the more experienced garou and kinfolk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1415896#post1415896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for raging you are right... if we follow the rules. But I would rather use a golden rule and allow the character go berserk (with all advantages and disadvantages) not changing the form. And role play it to the bone (maybe creating a hole in his soul for Wyrm to fill it).</div> </div> </div> </div>In our LARP there are special variants of Flaws like &quot;Cursed&quot; and such, that force Frenzy in other forms. But I'd rule that a character can't force this behaviour through willpower and therefore also not through a mental illness.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T07:32:31-07:00","id":1416988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1416750#post1416750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iirc, the taint isn't relevant for Erebus, since taint can be removed by &amp;quot;Rite of Cleansing&amp;quot; and other means, but an underlying impurity or even corruption can't.<br /> Also, it would be perfectly acceptable, to tie someone up, walk him to the gate of Erebus and throw him past the three-headed dog. As per the rules, the three-headed dog would not allow that person to leave Erebus again through its entrance, and the person once freed from his bonds would still need to travel through the entire Realm in search of the silver lake to exit. And plenty of guards on the way to offer &amp;quot;The Deal&amp;quot;. As far as I remember, they can be quite persuasive or forceful when offering the deal, so that chances are good, the person doesn't make it out.<br /> <br /> But, since the healing properties of Erebus are relatively unknown and it is regarded more like a hell by most garou (at least in the 1st Umbra book, iirc) it is unlikely that someone would do this.<br /> <br /> Also, most garou might try to heal such an afflicted garou. Not, themselves, but there are spirits, and therapists among the more experienced garou and kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course the taint isn't relevant for Erebus. But this &quot;impurity&quot; is rather an other Garou's opinion about this unfortunate, not the corruption of the soul per se. So Erebus can't help him. As for tying him up and throw him inside I think it won't work that way, because in that case Rite of the Silver Forge would be ridiculous. I think that Cerberus also would ignore him, as he is not one of the convicts. Of course, there's also the Deal, but the guards aren't forceful in that matter. They cannot force you to accept it, only tempt. Besides, using rope (even a fetish one) to put someone to the Silver Lake strips all the horror and mysticism of Erebus, don't you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T07:55:44-07:00","id":1416995,"title":"","content":"Well, the Rite of the Silver Forge is pretty, pretty rare, as only Charyss teaches it (well, I assume that she forbids those she teaches to re-teach it). So, since the realm is Hell to garou, I can totally see, that a pack has to bring a prisoner there, who the local sept wants punished severely. Prisoner Transport is a genre rarely applicable in WtA.<br /> And, I guess, the guards and them tempting the garou into &quot;The Deal&quot; only makes sense, if the garou can't just turn around and leave, because of Cerberus. But have to find their way to the lake and the castle and therefore the only valid exit, once they went past Cerberus. By that reasoning, damning one garou to Hell, by literally throwing him in there, seems as an appropriate means of punishment.<br /> <br /> And since the healing properties of Erebus aren't wildly known, but The Deal, the torture inflicted by the guards and such on the other hand are possibly wide spread legends, it makes sense for the garou who do the throwing to trust, that the damned garou they delivered would get punished. Which, iirc, isn't survived by many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 10-06-2020, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T08:10:41-07:00","id":1416997,"title":"","content":"As far as I know Rite of the Silver Forge is reserved only for the most vile criminals who otherwise would escaped punishment (as in the story I mentioned above). On other cases there are many other rites: The Hunt, Gaia's Vengeful Teeth or Rite of the Shattered Soul (which IMHO is stupid, cause it only adds more soldiers for Wyrm instead of allowing the fallen one to reborn in a more noble form). I also doubt that any of the sept leaders would risk an entire pack's lives to escort one Garou to Erebus (considering also that they also could accept the Deal and condemned themselves). I think those leaders would rather simply kill the crazy one.<br /> <br /> But the idea of delivering someone to Erebus to escape the problem and letting the convict return, stronger and full of anger strangely appael to me \ud83d\ude08. Especially if this Garou returns before the pack (he wasn't imprisoned, and they were punished by spirits the same way Ulysses was).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-06-2020, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T09:29:28-07:00","id":1417007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1416997#post1416997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know Rite of the Silver Forge is reserved only for the most vile criminals who otherwise would escaped punishment (as in the story I mentioned above).</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It isn't an option of a crazy person, but Erebus itself might be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1416997#post1416997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also doubt that any of the sept leaders would risk an entire pack's lives to escort one Garou to Erebus (considering also that they also could accept the Deal and condemned themselves).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why they don't go past the three-headed dog who guards the entrance, but throw the delinquent past him. Throwing a human or wolf body in Crinos form, should be fairly simple.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1416997#post1416997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think those leaders would rather simply kill the crazy one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from trying to therapy him, that is relatively likely, I guess. Or, they just leave him be and wait for circumstances to kill him in action. Which is the most likely thing if the ST doesn't intervene on his behalf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1416997#post1416997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the idea of delivering someone to Erebus to escape the problem and letting the convict return, stronger and full of anger strangely appael to me \ud83d\ude08. Especially if this Garou returns before the pack (he wasn't imprisoned, and they were punished by spirits the same way Ulysses was).</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible, if the pack enters the Realm with the convict proper, that might happen...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T11:33:24-07:00","id":1417025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1417007#post1417007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apart from trying to therapy him, that is relatively likely, I guess. Or, they just leave him be and wait for circumstances to kill him in action. Which is the most likely thing if the ST doesn't intervene on his behalf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the second option is highly unlikely. If they think about beheading him they rather won't wait for an oportunity to arise e. g. a battle. It would be too risky. They will rather kill him outright. <br /> <br /> I also think that throwing someone past the Cerberus is shallow. Even for Garou. Plus, if the lunatic unties himself and don't accept the Deal he could walk back as easily as he goes in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T13:45:27-07:00","id":1417047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1417025#post1417025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the second option is highly unlikely. If they think about beheading him they rather won't wait for an oportunity to arise e. g. a battle. It would be too risky. They will rather kill him outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd think it depends on the local septs morality and virtues.<br /> <br /> They might see killing him as a mercy. I would thing Red Talon, Get of Fenris, Shadowlords and their respective kinfolk would see it that way, and wonder, how he got Cliath rank in the first place.<br /> <br /> Others might think, that he is allowed to live and die as he pleases. If this mental illness isn't hindering him from participating in all the garou business the sept assigns to his pack and his pack mates are willing to take the additional risks of a partly unfit member, then okay. Fianna, Black Furies and some other tribes might take this approach.<br /> <br /> And Children of Gaia, Stargazer and possibly others might instead think that the extra effort to heal the person is (as long as a success seems possible) not covered by litany's &quot;tend sickness&quot; part and will yield more benefit in the long game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1417025#post1417025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that throwing someone past the Cerberus is shallow. Even for Garou. Plus, if the lunatic unties himself and don't accept the Deal he could walk back as easily as he goes in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your opinion. I find it witty. Also, it isn't that easy, given the umbral travel aspect to get there.<br /> <br /> I disagree that the person can walk out again, for as I read it, Cerberus will allow nobody out who has entered the cave system once, regardless of having accepted &quot;The Deal&quot; or not. So, the lunatic would have to travel through the whole cavern system to the silver lake and pass Charryse's judgement to be allowed to leave. So, he will be tempted multiple times by different guards he has to walk by to reach the exit. Or go even more insane by the screams and terrors he witnesses on his way there. If he gets lost, he might starve, or accept a Deal in exchange for food...<br /> <br /> In any case, now that I think of it, if he makes it to the lake, water of the lake offered to him by the ruler of the realm might bring forgetting and peace to his soul, effectively, if the ST agrees, removing the Flaws that are the problem in the first place. That said, since garou usually don't know about this properties, the wouldn't bring him there in the first place. But, iirc, one doesn't have to be tortured by the Brutes in Erebus to receive the healing. Reaching the Silver lake might be enough - or the rulers permission, maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T14:48:24-07:00","id":1417056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1415551-i-m-too-scared-to-shift?p=1417047#post1417047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd think it depends on the local septs morality and virtues.<br /> <br /> They might see killing him as a mercy. I would thing Red Talon, Get of Fenris, Shadowlords and their respective kinfolk would see it that way, and wonder, how he got Cliath rank in the first place.<br /> <br /> Others might think, that he is allowed to live and die as he pleases. If this mental illness isn't hindering him from participating in all the garou business the sept assigns to his pack and his pack mates are willing to take the additional risks of a partly unfit member, then okay. Fianna, Black Furies and some other tribes might take this approach.<br /> <br /> And Children of Gaia, Stargazer and possibly others might instead think that the extra effort to heal the person is (as long as a success seems possible) not covered by litany's &quot;tend sickness&quot; part and will yield more benefit in the long game.<br /> <br /> Well, your opinion. I find it witty. Also, it isn't that easy, given the umbral travel aspect to get there.<br /> <br /> I disagree that the person can walk out again, for as I read it, Cerberus will allow nobody out who has entered the cave system once, regardless of having accepted &quot;The Deal&quot; or not. So, the lunatic would have to travel through the whole cavern system to the silver lake and pass Charryse's judgement to be allowed to leave. So, he will be tempted multiple times by different guards he has to walk by to reach the exit. Or go even more insane by the screams and terrors he witnesses on his way there. If he gets lost, he might starve, or accept a Deal in exchange for food...<br /> <br /> In any case, now that I think of it, if he makes it to the lake, water of the lake offered to him by the ruler of the realm might bring forgetting and peace to his soul, effectively, if the ST agrees, removing the Flaws that are the problem in the first place. That said, since garou usually don't know about this properties, the wouldn't bring him there in the first place. But, iirc, one doesn't have to be tortured by the Brutes in Erebus to receive the healing. Reaching the Silver lake might be enough - or the rulers permission, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;(...)Cerberus will prevent the Unfortunates from escaping Erebus (...) The Unfortunates are garou or emanations of garou creatively tortured by the spirits of Erebus (...) All of the Unfortunates come to Erebus in their own way. The Rite of the Silver Forge forces some to Erebus. Many succumb to the temptation of the Deal. Others volountairly come to purge themselves of the taint of the Wyrm or to repent. (...)&quot;<br /> <br /> Umbra, the Velvet Shadow<br /> <br /> &quot;Non-Unfortunate visitors may also travel along the Banks of the river to the Citadel of Charyss (...) his (Cerberus) duty is to keep the damned souls in (...) getting out of Erebus is more difficult. The character must journey hrough the realm to the Citadel of Charyss (...)&quot;<br /> <br /> Umbra Revised<br /> <br /> &quot;(...) Cerberus decides who may enter the realm and for what purpose (...) If Cerberus doubts her intentions he instructs her to turn and walk back into the Umbra (...)<br /> <br /> W20 Umbra The Velvet Shadow <br /> <br /> So as you see tying and throwing is not an option. First of all, Cerberus cannot allow that, and if the lunatic reach The Citadel of Charyss without accepting the Deal she may even teach him the Rite of the Silver Forge so he could punish the ones who did that to him for their arrogance. As he is not one of the Unfortunates Cerberus will simply ignore him (but of course the entrance isn't the exit so this problem is irrelevant). He will not also have to pass the Charyss judgement cause he is not one of the Unfortunates so technically he is a visitor.<br /> <br /> And, going back to the original problem, I think that I found a perfect solution for it. As this is an Uktena sept they can use him regardless of his troubles: make him one of the Bane Tenders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 10-06-2020, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T15:05:21-07:00","id":1417059,"title":"","content":"You are right, I remembered it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}